//  3. CCS - 15/12/2025. Completed text update and now ready for final upload to Testflight before publishing; Please also note that I made formatting consistent (i.e spacing of tabs and added a blank line in between each prayer.
//  4. CCS - 15/12/2025. Updated Text for the "About" section : “A family that prays together stays together” - My Grandmother, Lola Mercy, believed this wholeheartedly. [Next paragraph] Mealtimes were always special at our household. Lola Mercy showed her love for us through the food she lovingly prepared and set on our table. Each meal would begin with a short prayer of thanks, aided by a set of prayer cards she picked up at a charity bazaar held at our church, many years ago. [Next paragraph] The same prayers are found here, to honor my Lola Mercy’s memory. It comes with the hope that the practice of saying grace will bring families closer, no matter where they may be. [Next paragraph] May God bless your family, bring you closer in spirit, and make you a blessing to everyone you meet. ~ Sabrina Angeline Cedo Sales
//  5. Question for SACS - would it be possible to add the "Previous" and "Next" buttons to the bottom of each prayer so that user will not have to scroll up again, for the prayers that are rather long? Please let me know.

import Foundation


let allPrayers = [
    
        Prayer(id: 0, text1: "Psalm 104: 14-15", text2: "You make grass grow for the cattle, and plants for man to use, so that he can grow his crops, and produce wine to make him happy, olive oil to make him cheerful and bread to give him strength.", text3: "Father of all creation, we thank you for all the gifts you lavish upon us every day. Bless those whose work produces what we eat and drink. Help us live in peace. Amen."),
      
      
      
        Prayer(id: 89, text1: "Matthew 11:19", text2: "When the Son of man came, he ate and drank, and everyone said, 'Look at this Man! He is a glutton and a wine drinker, a friend of tax collectors and other outcasts!' God’s wisdom, however, is shown to be true by its results.", text3: "O God, our Father, thank you for the gifts of friendship and intimacy nurtured by our eating together. Lord come and be seated at our table. Come, eat and drink with us. In the process, bring us your pardon, your love and your joy. Amen."),
      
        Prayer(id: 88, text1: "Luke 9:16", text2: "Jesus took the five loaves and two fish, looked up to heaven, thanked God for them, broke them, and gave them to his disciples to distribute to the people.", text3: "O God our Father, we praised and thank you for our daily sustenance. We praise you for our Lord Jesus, for his gifts of bread and gladness in the Holy Eucharist. Thank you, Father, for never abandoning us. Thank you for the love that reigns in our family. Thank you, Lord. Amen."),
      
        Prayer(id: 87, text1: "Mark 6:31", text2: "There were so many people coming and going that Jesus and his disciples didn’t even have time to eat. So, he said to them, 'Let us go off ourselves to some place where we will be alone and you can rest a while.'", text3: "O God our Father, you have designed our life to be rhythm of work, rest activity and prayer. We thank you Lord for giving us this time to rest and to share food and friendship. Bless all the things we do to make this a better and more humane world. Amen."),
      
        Prayer(id: 86, text1: "Luke 19:5-6", text2: "When Jesus came to that place, He looked up and said Zacchaeus, 'Hurry down, Zacchaeus, because I must stay in your house today.' Zacchaeus hurried down and welcomed him with great joy.", text3: "O God our loving Father, thank you for inviting us to your life of boundless joy. Lord Jesus, there is always a place for you at our table. Come every day; eat with us and increase our faith. We are happy to welcome you here. Amen."),
        
        Prayer(id: 85, text1: "Genesis 18:5", text2: "I will also bring a bit of food; it will give you strength to continue your journey. You have honored me by coming to my home, so let me serve you. They replied, 'Thank you; we accept.'", text3: "We thank you Lord for the food you give us to renew our strength. It enables us to continue our pilgrimage in this life. We pray that you bless each one of us. Amen."),
        
        Prayer(id: 84, text1: "Timothy 4:6", text2: "If you give these instructions to your brothers and sisters, you will be a good servant of Christ Jesus, as you feed yourself spiritually on the words of faith, and of the true teachings which you have followed.", text3: "O God, our Father, help us now and always to feed ourselves with Holy Scriptures. Bless our family with your peace emanating from our fidelity to your teaching. Amen."),
        
        Prayer(id: 83, text1: "Matthew 18:15", text2: "If your brother sins against you, go to him and show him his fault. But do it privately, just between yourselves. If he listens to you, you have won your brother back.'", text3: "Father, help us to live in harmony and peace. Give us your peace so we may understand each other and listen to each other in love. Teach us how to forgive one another. Bless the meal we eat today as we resolve to encourage one another in living Christianity to the fullest. Amen."),
        
        Prayer(id: 82, text1: "Luke 2: 51-52", text2: "So, Jesus went back with them to Nazareth, where he was obedient to them. His mother treasured all these things in her heart. Jesus grew in body and in wisdom, gaining favor with God and men.", text3: "Lord Jesus, bless us that we may always live in obedience to your will. We thank you for the inspiration and guidance of our parents which strengthens our faith and love for you. Amen."),
        
        Prayer(id: 81, text1: "Matthew 15:10-11", text2: "Then Jesus called the crowd to him and said to them, 'Listen and understand, it is not what goes into a person’s mouth that makes him ritually unclean; rather, what comes out of it makes him unclean.'", text3: "O God our loving Father, we praise and thank you for the built-in defenses in our body against disease and sickness. Lord cleanse our mouth that we may speak words of wisdom, forgiveness, kindness, justice and peace. May the meal we take today strengthen us so that we may serve and love you in others. Amen."),
        
        Prayer(id: 80, text1: "John 21: 5-6", text2: "Then he asked them, 'Young men, haven’t you caught anything?' 'Not a thing,' they answered. Then, he asked them, 'Throw your net out on the right side of the boat, and you will catch some.'", text3: "O God, our Father, without you we can do nothing. Bless this meal so that we can be responsive to your inspiration and challenge in our vocation, work or profession. Come and eat with us so we can enjoy your presence and receive your blessing. Amen."),
        
        Prayer(id: 79, text1: "Luke 19:9-10", text2: "Jesus said to him, “Salvation has come to this house today, for this man, is also a descendant of Abraham. The Son of Man came to seek and to save the lost.”", text3: "Come also to our house, Lord. Come with your salvation and your peace: we have great need of them. Bless our family and bless the meal you are providing for us today. Amen."),
      
        Prayer(id: 78, text1: "Luke 14:16-17", text2: "Jesus said to him, “There was once a man who was giving a great feast to which he invited many people. When it was time for the feast he sent his servant to tell his guests, “Come, everything is ready!”", text3: "Lord, we are together here to celebrate your goodness manifested concretely in our meal. May this remind us of your invitation to share your life in heaven, the banquet of love and justice. Bless the hands that prepared this meal. Bless all our priests who enable us to partake the Eucharistic meals. Amen."),
        
        Prayer(id: 77, text1: "Proverbs 23:1-3", text2: "When you sit down to eat with an important man, keep in mind who he is. If you have big appetite, restrain yourself. Don’t be greedy for the fine foods he serves; he may be trying to trick you.", text3: "Lord let our lives not be ruled by ambition. Give us a simplicity and a humility of heart which will enable us to do without and enable us to serve others. Bless our family: we love you above all things. Amen."),
        
        Prayer(id: 76, text1: "John 6:32", text2: "“I am telling you the truth,” Jesus said, “What Moses gave you was not the bread from heaven; It is my Father who gives you the real bread from heaven.”", text3: "Blessed are you Father for giving us our daily bread. Blessed are you for the Holy Eucharist which strengthens our faith, increases our hope and nourishes our love. Amen."),
            Prayer(id: 75, text1: "Acts 2:46", text2: "Day after day they met as a group in the Temple, and they had their meals together in their homes, eating with glad and humble hearts.", text3: "Lord, we come in your name to take our meal together. Guide us to discover the joy of a humble and simple style of living. Amen."),
        
        Prayer(id: 74, text1: "Luke 22:15-16", text2: "He said to them, “I have wanted so much to eat the Passover meal with you before I suffer. For I tell you, I will never eat it until it is given its full meaning in the Kingdom of God.”", text3: "Lord, you are here as our guest and the source of our strength. Come and share what we have on the table. Make faith the guide of our life and hope our encouragement. Bring us together again at the banquet in your Kingdom. Amen."),
        
        Prayer(id: 73, text1: "Luke 5:30-31", text2: "Some Pharisees and some teachers of the Law, who belonged to their group complained to Jesus’ disciples, “Why do you eat and drink with tax collectors and other outcasts?” they asked. Jesus answered them, “People, who are well do not need a doctor, but only those who are sick.”", text3: "Come Lord; make this meal a healing balm for our wounded hearts. Enable us to accept each other and to increase our love. Give us the resolve to serve our brothers and sisters and the faith to see you in their faces. Amen."),
        
        Prayer(id: 72, text1: "Romans 12:13", text2: "Share your belongings with your needy fellow Christians and open your homes to strangers.", text3: "O God, our Father, as we enjoy this tasty meal, guide us to make our house a welcoming home and to share what we have with the poor and the suffering. Bless us with a generous heart and cheerful spirit. Bless our family. Amen."),
        
        Prayer(id: 71, text1: "John 2:10", text2: "“Everyone else serves the best wine first, and after the guests have drunk a lot, he serves the ordinary wine. But you have kept the best wine until now!\"", text3: "O God our Father, you have intended the beauty and the abundance of creation to be shared and enjoyed. Touch our self-centered hearts that we may stop hoarding our talents and resources. Thank you, Father, for giving us your Son Jesus Christ. He provided us with the example of generosity. Bring joy into our family life and give us the strength to overcome obstacles in practicing love. Amen."),
        
        Prayer(id: 70, text1: "Deuteronomy 15:11", text2: "There will always be poor people in the land. Therefore, I command you to be openhanded toward your neighbors, who are poor and needy in your land.", text3: "O God our Father, because of selfishness, many suffer, hunger, and thirst. There is enough for everyone’s need but not everyone’s greed. Lord God, make us aware of what other people need. Teach us to share what we have and never to tire in our effort to secure justice for everyone. Bless our meal; bless our family. Amen."),
        
        Prayer(id: 69, text1: "Luke 6:20-21", text2: "Jesus looked at his disciples and said “Happy are you poor, the Kingdom of God is yours! Happy are you who are hungry now; you will be filled.”", text3: "O God our Father, we praise and thank you for our experience of hunger. Our experience of hunger for truth and justice is from you. Give us one day, the blessing of seeing your Kingdom. May this meal give us strength so we will be better able to serve you. Amen."),
        
        Prayer(id: 68, text1: "Luke 7:36", text2: "A Pharisee invited Jesus to have dinner with him and Jesus went to his house and sat down to eat.", text3: "Come to our house today, Lord. Happily, and humbly, we will welcome you. Bless the food we are about to receive in your name. Amen."),
        
        Prayer(id: 67, text1: "Luke 15:2", text2: "The Pharisees and the teachers of the law started to grumble. “This man welcomes outcast and even eats with them.”", text3: "O God our Father may your unconditional love enable us to be impartial and unbiased in our relationships. Lord, come eat with us. We need your love and your presence; we need your strength and your pardon. Give us faith to recognize you here among us. Lord, be with us. Amen."),
        
        Prayer(id: 66, text1: "John 6:11", text2: "Jesus took the bread, gave thanks to God and distributed it to the people who were sitting there.", text3: "We give thanks to you, Lord, for the bread you give us. We give thanks to you, Lord, for helping us to share our food. Amen."),
        
        Prayer(id: 65, text1: "Isaiah 58:7", text2: "Share your food with the hungry and open your homes to the homeless poor. Give clothes to those who have nothing to wear, and do not refuse to help your own relatives.", text3: "Lord, give us a welcoming heart so we will be free to share our food and our love with others. Help us recognize you in the face of every poor and unloved person in this world, especially in our family. We ask you, Lord, to bless our meal and our family. Amen."),
        
        Prayer(id: 64, text1: "Deuteronomy 8:3", text2: "He made you go hungry, and then he gave you manna to eat, food that you and your ancestors had never eaten before. He did this to teach you that man must not depend on bread alone to sustain him, but on everything that the Lord says.", text3: "Lord, feed us with your word, which nourishes us and makes us grow. We ask for the grace of listening to you every day, and to really listen that we may understand each other more. Bless our family, Lord. Amen."),
        
        Prayer(id: 63, text1: "Luke 14:13", text2: "“When you give a feast, invite the poor, the crippled, the lame, and the blind; and you will be blest.”", text3: "Lord, we wish to keep the doors of our home open to welcome anyone who is looking for kindness and hospitality. Help us be willing to share the food on our table with people who have the need for it. Give us the blessing of your love. Amen."),
        
        Prayer(id: 62, text1: "Acts 14:17", text2: "But he has always given evidence of his existence by the good things he does, “He gives you rain from heaven and crops at the right times; He gives you food and fills your hearts with happiness.”", text3: "God our Father, all we have comes from you. Help us enjoy your countless gifts and blessings with simplicity. May the spirit of joy and gratitude urge us to share what we have generously. Bless our meal today. Amen."),
        
        Prayer(id: 61, text1: "Luke 22:27", text2: "“Who is greater - The one who sits down to eat or the one who serves him? The one who sits down, of course. But I am among you as one who serves.”", text3: "Lord Jesus, you came to serve us in humility. We thank you for your goodness and your example in dying to self. Teach us how to serve our family and others joyfully. Guide us in how to respect and be appreciative of those who serve us. Amen."),
        
        Prayer(id: 60, text1: "Revelation 19:9", text2: "Then the angel said to me, “Write this: Happy are those who have been invited to the wedding feast of the Lamb.” And the angel added, “These are the true words of God.”", text3: "Lord, our God, thank you for bringing us together around this table. Thank you for inviting us to the wedding banquet of Jesus at the Holy Eucharist, which is a foretaste of heaven. He is the Lamb who feeds us and makes us holy. Thank you, Lord. Amen."),
        
        Prayer(id: 59, text1: "Luke 10:8-9", text2: "Whenever you go into a town and are made welcome, eat what is set before you, heal the sick in that town, and say to the people there, “The kingdom of God has come near you.”", text3: "Lord Jesus, we are your disciples. May our lifestyle and attitude radiate love in fields, in factories, offices, and homes to show that the kingdom of God is now near. May the purpose of our eating be to gain strength to serve you better. Amen."),
        
        Prayer(id: 58, text1: "Matthew 14:17", text2: "All we have here are five loaves and two fish.” They replied.", text3: "O God our Father, we present to you our strength as well as our limitations. Use them, Lord, to feed the different hungers of humanity. Let them be the raw materials of your miracles of love. Amen."),
        
        Prayer(id: 57, text1: "Ezekiel 18:7-8", text2: "He doesn’t cheat or rob anymore. He returns what a borrower gives him as security: he feeds and gives clothing to the naked. He doesn’t lend money for profit. He refuses to do evil and gives an honest decision in any dispute.", text3: "O God our Father, we praise and thank you for your grace which enables us to live virtuously according to your command. Lord, as we strive to do our daily duties, we look forward to a new world where every person will have enough to eat and drink and be properly clothed. Give us fortitude not to drift away from your entrusted vocation and mission to us. Amen."),
        
        Prayer(id: 56, text1: "Matthew 18:21-22", text2: "Then Peter came to Jesus and asked, “Lord, If my brother keeps on sinning against me, how many times do I have to forgive him? Seven times?” “No, not seven times,” answered Jesus, “but seventy times seven.”", text3: "Lord, help us live in genuine friendship; to show affection, to overcome our problems, and to forgive each other. Bless the meal we are going to eat which is a symbol of our fellowship. Amen."),
        
        Prayer(id: 55, text1: "Jeremiah 31:12-13", text2: "They will come and sing for joy on Mount Zion and be delighted with my gifts. Gifts of grain and wine and olive oil, gifts of sheep and cattle. They will have everything they need.", text3: "O God our Father, we want to express our delight in being together to enjoy your good gifts. Give us the strength we need to meet our daily responsibilities. Let us announce the salvation you have brought, by our loving care and assistance to others. Amen."),
        
        Prayer(id: 54, text1: "1 Timothy 6:7-8", text2: "What did we bring into the world? Nothing! What can we take out of the world? Nothing! So then, if we have food and clothes, that should be enough for us.", text3: "Father, you are our life now and forever. In you, we place all our trust. Let your Holy Spirit constantly remind us that we are just pilgrims on earth. Thank you for making us your sons and daughters and thank you for all the gifts you lavish upon us every day. Bless our meal. Amen."),
        
        Prayer(id: 53, text1: "Amos 8:11", text2: "The time is coming when I will send famine on the land. People will be hungry, but not for bread; they will hunger and thirst for a message from the Lord. I, the Sovereign Lord, have spoken.", text3: "Our Father, give us hunger for a message from you that will bring hope into our life. Give us a thirst for you that will move us to serve our brothers and sisters. Bless our family gathered here today. Amen."),
        
        Prayer(id: 52, text1: "Luke 14:23-24", text2: "So, the master said to the servant, “Go out to the country roads and lanes and make people come in, so that my house will be full. I tell you that none of those men who were invited will taste my banquet!”", text3: "O God our Father, we praise and thank you for the gift of faith. Lord, our answer to your invitation is YES. We are not very strong, and so we need to be nourished with your strength. Thank you for asking us. Amen."),
        
        Prayer(id: 51, text1: "Genesis 9:3", text2: "Now you can eat them, as well as green plants; I give them all to you for food.", text3: "We thank you, God, our Father, because in your love you have given us rich sources of food. Thank you for your special kindness in providing this meal for us today. Amen."),
        
        Prayer(id: 50, text1: "Luke 22:14-15", text2: "When the hour came, Jesus took his place at the table with the apostles. He said to them, “I have wanted so much to eat this Passover meal with you before I suffer.”", text3: "O God our Father, we praise and thank you for the gift of time which enables us to enjoy each other’s company. Lord Jesus Christ, the table is ready, and we invite you to be with us today. Give us the blessing of faith, especially when we experience suffering and loneliness. Keep our family in the security of your love. Amen."),
        
        Prayer(id: 49, text1: "Matthew 10:42", text2: "And if anyone gives even a cup of cold water to one of these little ones who is my disciple, truly I tell you, that person will certainly not lose their reward.", text3: "Lord Jesus it is hard for us to recognize you in suffering people, in the young or the old Through your grace bless us so that we may serve you through these people Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 48, text1: "Luke 12:37", text2: "How happy are those servants whose master finds them awake and ready when he returns! I tell you he will take off his coat, have then sit down, and will wait on them.", text3: "O God our Father thank you for your confidence in us We thank you for the countless times you have come to serve our family in many ways through our loved ones and friends Thank you most specially for this meal you are serving us at our table Bless this food and our family Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 47, text1: "John 6:51", text2: "I am the living bread that came down from heaven If anyone eats this bread, he will live forever.", text3: "God our Father thank you for planting in our hearts the yearning for eternal life Thank you for giving us our needs by living among us today in Holy Scriptures and in the Holy Eucharist Only when we are close to him that we’ll have the strength to live joyfully Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 46, text1: "Revelation 3:20", text2: "Listen! I stand at the door and knock; If anyone hears my voice and opens the door, I will come into his house and eat with him, and he will eat with me.", text3: "O God our Father we praise and thank you for not abandoning us though we tend to take your love for granted Lord our friend we open the doors of our home to you We would like for you to eat with us Let your word inspire us every day Bless the food we are going to eat Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 45, text1: "Proverbs 15:17", text2: "Better to eat vegetable with people you love than to eat the finest meat where there is hate.", text3: "God our loving Father fill us with your love so that we may grow in unity and friendship Help us to live simply and to be generous Bless this family who loves you Lord Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 44, text1: "Isaiah 55:2-3", text2: "Why spend money on what does not satisfy? Why spend your wages and still be hungry? Listen to me and do what I say, and you will enjoy the best food of all. Listen now my people, and come to me; come to me, and you will have life. I will make a lasting covenant with you the blessings I promised David.", text3: "Heavenly Father every day you satisfy our hunger and thirst not only with material food and drink but with your love Help us meet gladly the needs of our brothers and sisters Teach us how to work for the realization of your kingdom Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 43, text1: "Ecclesiastes 9:7", text2: "Go ahead eat your food and be happy; drink your wine and be cheerful It is God’s approval of your work.", text3: "Lord our God we praise and thank you for the gift of nourishment and the gift of joy May our lives express our gratitude for the food and drink you give us. Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 42, text1: "Proverbs 9:5-6", text2: "Come eat my food and drink the wine that I have mixed. Leave the company of ignorant people, and live. Follow the way of knowledge,", text3: "God our Father, thank you for the nourishing food set before us. May it give us strength to pursue what is good true and beautiful in life. Enable us to inspire others to know and love you each day Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 41, text1: "Matthew 6:11-12", text2: "Give us this day our daily bread. Forgive us for our sins, just as we have forgiven those who sinned against us.", text3: "Thank you Lord for bringing us together to eat what you provide for us every day. Teach us we pray, to offer the food of forgiveness to each other Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 40, text1: "Genesis 1:11", text2: "Then he commanded, “Let the earth produce all kinds of plants those that bear grain and those that bear fruit”- and it was done.", text3: "We exalt you Father for all the things you have created for us. Give us the determination to work conscientiously and cheerfully that everyone may enjoy its fruits. Bless us Lord. Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 39, text1: "Matthew 5:13", text2: "You are like salt for all mankind. But if salt loses its saltiness, there is no way to make it salty again. It has become worthless, so it is thrown out and people trample on it.", text3: "Lord, May the testimony of our words and our life be like salt which gives savor and meaning to life. Let the food we are going to eat strengthen us, so our energies do not fail. Give us the blessing of your power and your joy. Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 38, text1: "Matthew 7:11", text2: "So if you sinful people know how to give good gifts to your children, how much more will your heavenly Father give good gifts to those who ask him.", text3: "O God our Father, we pray for our family: help us know how to love and respect each other and to strive for unity. Give us the food and the love we need to live. Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 37, text1: "Leviticus 23:17", text2: "Each family is to bring two loaves of bread and present them to the Lord as a special gift. Each loaf shall be made of four pounds of flour baked with yeast and shall be presented to the Lord as an offering of the first grain to be harvested.", text3: "Thank you Lord, for bringing us together again around this table. Through your goodness we have this meal to offer, which earth has given and human hands have made. Sanctify and bless them. Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 36, text1: "1 Corinthians 10:16", text2: "The cup we use in the Lord’s supper and for which we give thanks to God; when we drink from it, we are sharing in the blood of Christ. And the bread we break; when we eat it, we are sharing in the body of Christ.", text3: "O God our Father, Your Trinitarian life with your Son and the Holy Saints is a fellowship of love and sharing. Lord Jesus Christ, we wish to be closely united in your love and goodness. Bless us with your peace. Help us live in communion with one another. Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 35, text1: "Psalm 132: 14-15", text2: "This is where I will live forever; This is where I want to rule. I will richly provide Zion with all she needs; I will satisfy her poor with food.", text3: "O God, our Father we praise and thank you for the gift of Christian life, which enable us to relish the joy of being your chosen children. Lord our Father, abide with us and help us do what pleases you in our words and deeds. Bless our food. May our generosity enable the poor to be filled with your abundant graces. Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 34, text1: "Luke 3:11", text2: "Whoever has two shirts must give one to the man who has none, and whoever has food must share it.", text3: "O God, our Father thank you for our shelter and clothing. We thank you, Lord of God for the meal you are giving us today. Help us share we have with the needy. Bless us generous and just. Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 33, text1: "John 6:56", text2: "Whoever eats my flesh and drinks my blood lives in me and I live in him.", text3: "O God, our Father, we are amazed how the food we eat become part of our body. It is more marvelous to realize that receiving Jesus in Holy Communion, we become like Him in our capacity to love. Bless us Lord, with the power of His love. Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 32, text1: "Psalm 36:7-8", text2: "How precious O God is your constant love! We find protection under the shadows of your wings. We feast on the abundant food you provide. You let us drink from the river of your goodness.", text3: "O God our father we praise and thank you for your constant providence and protection. We want to thank you Father most holy, because through our family, we feel the love you have for us. Unite us ever more closely to one another. Bless this food which we will eat together in your name. Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 31, text1: "Genesis 3:19", text2: "By the sweat of your brow, will you have food to eat, until you return to the ground from which you were made. For you were made from dust, and to dust you will return.", text3: "We praise you Lord for aiding us to earn our daily bread. Help us that our work may be the source of our joy and fulfillment. Teach us to share our love and food with those who have none. Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 30, text1: "1 Corinthians 10:17", text2: "Because there is one loaf of bread, all of us though many, are one body, for we all share the same loaf.", text3: "Thank you Lord for making all of us different and yet one with you, around this table. Thank you for the food set before us which will unite and spur us to work together for the realization of your Kingdom. Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 29, text1: "John 2:1-2", text2: "On the third day, a wedding took place at Cana in Galilee. Jesus’ mother was there, and Jesus and his disciples had also been invited to the wedding.", text3: "O God our Father, we praised and thank you for the Sacrament of Marriage. Lord Jesus, we invite you together with our blessed Mother, to share our family joys as we eat together. This is your home and we are your family. Lord bless us. Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 28, text1: "2 Corinthians 9:10", text2: "And God, who supplies seed for the Sower and bread to eat, will also supply you with all the seed you need, and will make it grow and produce a rich harvest from your generosity.", text3: "Father, we are grateful for all you have given to our family: we bless you for everything. Help us to always share what we have, Thank you for this meal. Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 27, text1: "Isaiah 30:23", text2: "Whenever you plant crops, the Lord will send rain to make them grow a rich harvest, and your cattle will have plenty of pasture.", text3: "O God our Father we praise and thank you for the fruitfulness of all our endeavors. May you be praised Lord, for the wisdom and the beauty in all you have made. Thank you for everything in nature and creation that sustains us. Bless this food which comes to us from your hand. Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 26, text1: "John 6:55", text2: "For my flesh is the real food; my blood is the real drink.", text3: "God our Father, thank you for giving us Jesus as our daily Bread. Lord, while we are here to eat and drink, enable us to be the food of love and joy to each other. Guide us to meet the deep and real needs of our brothers and sisters. Bless us today. Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 25, text1: "John 66:27", text2: "Do not work for food that spoils; instead, work for the food that lasts for eternal life.", text3: "O God our Father we praise and thank you for providing for all our needs. Lord Jesus, at our family table today, guide us to balance the pursuit of material and spiritual food. Give us the wisdom and the strength to pursue what is heavenly and pleasing to you, our God. Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 24, text1: "Acts 10:40-41", text2: "But God raised him from death three days later, and caused him to appear, not to everyone, but only to the witnesses that God had already chosen, that is to us, who ate and drank with him, after he rose from death.", text3: "Lord Jesus Christ, the way we live in this world bears witness to your resurrection. Come eat and drink with us, and give us the courage we need to proclaim that you live. Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 23, text1: "Luke 22:28-30", text2: "You have stayed with me all through my trials; and just as my Father has given me the right to rule, so I will give you the same right. You will eat and drink at my table in my Kingdom, and you will sit on thrones to rule over the twelve tribes of Israel.", text3: "We thank you Lord Jesus Christ, for inviting us to eat and drink at your table in your Kingdom. We wish our meal today to be a sign of the companionship that awaits us. Bless us Lord. Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 22, text1: "Mark 14:14-15", text2: "Follow him to the house he enters and say to the owner of the house. “The teacher says, “Where is the room where my disciples and I will eat the Passover meal? Then he will show you a large upstairs room, fixed up and furnished, where you will get everything for us.”", text3: "Lord Jesus Christ, bless those who prepared this meal with love. Be with us in joy and in gratitude. Bless the food we have as we praise you forever and ever. Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 21, text1: "Matthew 7:24-25", text2: "Anyone who hears these words of mine and obeys them, is like a wise man who built his house on rock. The rain poured down, the rivers flooded over, and the wind blew hard against that house. But it did not fall, because it was built on rock.", text3: "Lord we want to build our family upon you. Give us the grace to remain faithful to you in spite of all our trials. Keep us united in knowing that you are present in our lives. Bless the meal we are going to eat. Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 20, text1: "Corinthians 10:16", text2: "The cup we use in the Lord’s Supper and for which we give thanks to God; when we drink from it, we are sharing in the blood of Christ. And the bread we break when we eat it, we are sharing in the body of Christ.", text3: "O God our Father, we praise and thank you for our friends and for our family. Lord Jesus Christ, we acknowledge your loving presence among us as we come together for this meal. Help us to live in unity as your brothers and sisters and let this love flow to our relationship with persons we meet outside our home. Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 19, text1: "Luke 14:15", text2: "When one of the men sitting at the table heard this he said to Jesus, “How happy are those who will sit down at the feast in the kingdom of God!”", text3: "Lord, we who are seated at this table, are invited to your Kingdom of joy and friendship. Help us that we may build this harmony here on earth. Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 18, text1: "Proverbs 17:1", text2: "Better to eat a dry crust of bread with peace of mind than a banquet in a house full of trouble.", text3: "O God our Father, we praise and thank you for the gift of contentment which enables us to relish whatever food you send us. Prevent us from the evils of gluttony, lust and greed. Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 17, text1: "Genesis 28:20-21", text2: "Then Jacob made a vow, saying, “If God will be with me, and keep me safe during my journey, give me bread to eat and clothing to put on, so that I come back to my father\'s house in peace, then the LORD shall be my God”.", text3: "Father, You are our God, too. We exalt you for being with us and protecting us in our life’s journey. We praise you for welcoming us so kindly. Bless and strengthen us: we pray through Jesus Christ our Lord. Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 16, text1: "Genesis 1:29", text2: "I have provided all kinds of grain and all kinds of fruit for you to eat.", text3: "O God our Father, blessed are you for this bread which earth has given, and human hands have made. As we enjoy this meal, remind us to be thankful and appreciate all those who were instrumental in the production and in the cooking of this food. Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 15, text1: "Matthew 5:6", text2: "Happy are those whose greatest desire is to do what God requires; God will satisfy them fully!", text3: "O God, our Father, your tremendous love is the answer to our ceaseless yearning. Enable us to perceive in our hunger for food, a much deeper hunger for you and your Kingdom. Bless our Family always. Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 14, text1: "John 6:35", text2: "“I am the Bread of Life”, Jesus told them. “He who comes to me will never be hungry; he who believes in me will never be thirsty.”", text3: "Lord Jesus Christ, you alone can satisfy our yearning for life and love. Be our food and drink. Help us live in communion with you. Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 13, text1: "Isaiah 25:6", text2: "Here on Mount Zion, the Lord Almighty will prepare a banquet for all the nations of the world - a banquet of the richest food and the finest wine.", text3: "Lord our God, guide us towards the banquet in your Kingdom where we will abide in lasting joy. Until then, in your kindness, please stay close to us to protect us. Blessed are you. Lord. Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 12, text1: "Matthew 5:23-24", text2: "So, if you are about to offer your gift to God at the altar, and remember that your brother has something against you, leave your gift there in front of the altar, and go at once and make peace with your brother.", text3: "O God our Father because of our frail human nature, we sometimes hurt each other’s feelings. Give us the grace to be more considerate, understanding and gentle in our ways. Please show us how to forgive each other so that we can be united around this table. Continue to give us your blessing of love and humility. Amen"),

        Prayer(id: 11, text1: "John 21:12-13", text2: "Jesus said to them, “Come and eat.” None of the disciples dared ask him, “Who are you?” because they knew it was the Lord. So, Jesus went over, took the bread, and gave it to them; he did the same with the fish.", text3: "Lord Jesus, you have risen and live among us. We often cannot see you clearly. When we eat together, enable us to experience how close you are to us. Bless us Lord, and bless our work with fruitfulness. Amen"),

        Prayer(id: 10, text1: "Luke 22:19-20", text2: "Then he took a piece of bread, gave thanks to God, broke it and gave it to them, saying - “This is my body, which is given to you. Do this in memory of me.” In the same way, he gave them the cup, after supper saying - “This cup is God’s new covenant, sealed with my blood, which is poured for you.”", text3: "Lord Jesus, as we eat this meal, we thank you for being so good in giving yourself up for us.  Thank you for the people who constantly offer themselves, that we might live in serenity and with sense of security. Thank you for your generosity. Amen"),

        Prayer(id: 9, text1: "Job 31:16-17", text2: "I have never refused the appeals of the poor, or let widows give up hope, while looking for help. I have not kept my food to myself, but have given it to the orphans. ", text3: "O God, our Father it is your will that we all enjoy the bounty of creation. Help us share whatever we have with the poor. Blessed us with your love. Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 8, text1: "Deuteronomy 11:13-14", text2: "So then, obey the commands that I have given you today; love the Lord your God, and serve Him with all your Heart. He will then send rain on your land in its season, both autumn and spring rains, so that you may gather in your grain, new wine and olive oil.", text3: "Lord God, we desire to love you above all things. Help us because we are weak, and easily forget about you. Thank you for not forgetting us. Thank you for the air, the rain, for family and friends, and for this meal, which we are going to have in your name. Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 7, text1: "Isaiah 30:20", text2: "“The Lord will make you go through hard times, but he himself will be there to teach you, and you will not have to search for him anymore.”", text3: "Lord, God of comfort and hope, enable us to overcome all our trials and difficulties. May we one day gaze upon your face in heaven, where there is no sorrow and no tears. To you be honor and glory forever. Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 6, text1: "Matthew 6:26", text2: "Look at the birds of the air; they do not sow or reap or store away in barns, and yet your heavenly Father feeds them. Are you not much more valuable than they?", text3: "God, our Father, we are your children and you know us perfectly, you know our needs. Please remove all our worries and our fears. Thank you for the gift of your loving care and our daily food. Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 5, text1: "Proverbs 22:9", text2: "Be generous and share your food with the poor. You will be blessed for it.", text3: "Lord, our God, remove all jealousy, envy and selfishness from us. Help us treat each other generously and affectionately. Make us willing to share what we have. Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 4, text1: "Matthew 25:34-36", text2: "Come and possess the Kingdom, which has been prepared for you, ever since the creation of the world. I was hungry and you fed me, thirsty, and you gave me a drink; I was a stranger and you received me in your homes.", text3: "Thank you Lord, for giving us what we have here to eat and drink. Let this meal soften our hearts to the needs of other people. Guide us to be hospitable and generous as we recognize you in every needy person. Make us understand how our lives are bound together by your love for us.  Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 3, text1: "John 4:32-34", text2: "But he answered, “I have food to eat that you know nothing about.” So, the disciples started asking among themselves, “Could somebody have brought him food?” Jesus said to them, “My food is to obey the will of the One who sent me and to finish the work he gave me to do.”", text3: "O God, our Father, you have sent your Son to guide us and to look for things that money cannot buy. Lord Jesus, may your joy in doing the will of God, our Father, be our food too. We thank you for giving us this meal today. Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 2, text1: "Luke 15:17-18", text2: "At last, he came to his senses and said “All my father’s hired workers have more than they can eat, and here I am about to starve. I will get up and go to my father and say, “Father, I have sinned against God and against you.”", text3: "Father of goodness, may the meal we are going to have open our eyes and our hearts to your goodness and forgiveness. We thank you for always welcoming us back, despite our weaknesses and unfaithfulness. Thank you for giving us hope! Amen."),

        Prayer(id: 1, text1: "Luke 15:22-24", text2: "But the father called to his servants. “Hurry!” he said. Bring the best robe and put it on him. Put a ring on his finger and shoes on his feet. Then go and get the prize calf and kill it, and let us celebrate with a feast! For this son of mine was dead but now he is alive; he was lost but now he has been found.\" And so the feasting began.", text3: "Thank you Father, for always being glad to welcome us back, despite our sinfulness. We are grateful for teaching us how to accept each other’s uniqueness. Enable us to have the foretaste of the joys in heaven, through our mutual encouragement and affirmation of your love. Bless our meal. Amen.")

    
]
